:"2748","md5":"613249d5a4773798b0e3961a0035226a","crc32":"8ca7ed87","sha1":"96a9cd091a33759779e18a655ef3ae0eba35c03e","format":"Metadata"}],"files_count":15,"item_last_updated":1727726159,"item_size":64094467,"metadata":{"identifier":"arranged-will-fritch_202409","mediatype":"audio","collection":["du-participatory-archive","audio_music"],"creator":"Gus Baxter","date":"2024-09-27","description":"In this episode of The Bravery Blueprint, host Gus Baxter interviews Will Fritch, a graduate of Drew University's 4+1 program, who shares his insights on balancing optimism and the reality of failure. Will discusses how his experience as a baseball player, particularly after tearing his ACL, taught him the importance of resilience, embracing failure, and consistently putting in the work without immediate results. He emphasizes the value of networking, surrounding oneself with positive influences, and maintaining a growth mindset. Will's approach to challenges, driven by his competitive nature and passion for self-improvement, serves as a blueprint for navigating both personal and professional life.<div><br /></div><div><b>CREDITS</b></div><div><br /></div><div>The Bravery Blueprint is hosted and written by Gus Baxter with original music and audio engineering by Logan Flores</div><div><br /></div><div><em style=\"color:rgb(44,44,44);font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:14px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);\">Subscribe to this podcast and leave a review on Spotify, Apple Podcasts, or wherever you get podcasts! Discover more <a href=\"https://www.wmnjradio.com/\" style=\"background:transparent;color:rgb(75,100,255);\" rel=\"nofollow\">WMNJ</a> and <a href=\"https://duparchive.org/\" style=\"background:transparent;color:rgb(75,100,255);\" rel=\"nofollow\">DUPA</a> content at <a href=\"https://www.wmnjradio.com/\" style=\"background:transparent;color:rgb(75,100,255);\" rel=\"nofollow\">wmnjradio.com</a> and <a href=\"https://duparchive.org/\" styl